There's a hack-style game on our system called 'omega' which features
The Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch.  In this game it is given to those
who achieve rank in the Order of Paladins.  Unfortunately there is
no corresponding rabbit. (There is a rabbit in the game 
but I don't think it has anything to do with the grenade)  In 'omega'
one must count to 5 (I mean three) before pulling the pin.  The projectile
is lodged at the foe who is utterly annialited, along with his corpse and
the person who threw is covered with gore (this has no apparent impact).
A device like this could be easily adapted to nethack, perhaps as
gift from one's god. Perhaps the rabbit, whose only bane is the grenade,
could be the guard to a cavern in which is contained the last words
which guide the adventurer to some useful object.  Of course, when one
finally reaches the treasure, the Keystone Kops would also arrive on the
scene.
(For those who do not understand, rent "Monty Python and the Holy Grail").
 
 BTW, omega, though an extremely buggy game, does have some nice features.
 One thing I like is the ability to use wands/staff/projectiles in something
 other than a straight line.  This is similar to the way one choses
 teleportation position in nethack.  Perhaps a similar feature could be
 put into nethack, esp for projectiles. Maybe some of the same code could be
 used to make this adaptation.


